# Agent Skills Routing

How global agent skills and MCP tools are prioritized. Skills install machine-local; this rule syncs per project so every agent session follows the same routing.

---

## The Rule

**Global skills (`-g`) are already available in every workspace** — new and existing — without per-project install. Cursor exposes skill *descriptions* automatically; the agent reads full `SKILL.md` only when a task matches.

**Do not try to pre-load all skills.** ~70 skill descriptions compete for context. Load one primary skill per domain; use MCP tools when the task needs live catalog data.

**MCP servers** in `~/.cursor/mcp.json` are machine-global. Restart Cursor after changes. Auth via `~/.zshrc` env vars (see `cursor-sync.md`).

---

## Layer Model

| Layer | Location | Every project? | Pre-loaded? |
|-------|----------|----------------|-------------|
| vibeCodingRules | `<project>/.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | After copy/sync | `alwaysApply: true` rules only |
| Global skills | `~/.agents/skills/` (CLI store) + **`~/.cursor/skills/`** (Cursor personal — symlink bridge; see `cursor-sync.md`) | Yes (same machine) | Descriptions yes; full skill on trigger |
| Global MCP | `~/.cursor/mcp.json` | Yes (same machine) | Tool defs when MCP connected |

**New machine:** run skill installs + MCP setup from `cursor-sync.md` once, then copy rules (including this file) into each project.

---

## Priority Matrix (when multiple skills match)

Use **one primary** per row. Read secondary only if primary is insufficient or user names it.

| Domain | Primary | Secondary | Deprioritize / skip |
|--------|---------|-----------|---------------------|
| **Coding standards** | vibeCodingRules (`AGENTS.md` routing) | — | Never override with skills |
| **UI layout + design system** | `ui-ux-pro-max` | `design-taste-frontend` | `minimalist-ui`, `industrial-brutalist-ui`, `high-end-visual-design` unless user picks antique/bold style |
| **UI audit / a11y** | `web-design-guidelines` | `frontend-design` | — |
| **UI redesign (existing app)** | `redesign-existing-projects` | `design-taste-frontend` | — |
| **shadcn components** | 21st MCP + `21st-registry` | `shadcn-ui` MCP | `animated-component-libraries` unless Magic UI / React Bits named |
| **GSAP API** | `gsap-core` → `gsap-timeline` → `gsap-scrolltrigger` | `gsap-react` (React) | — |
| **Scroll (non-GSAP)** | `scroll-reveal-libraries` (simple) | `locomotive-scroll`, `barba-js` | — |
| **Framer Motion** | `motion-framer` | `vercel-react-view-transitions` | — |
| **Three.js (vanilla)** | `threejs-webgl` | — | `babylonjs-engine`, `playcanvas-engine` unless named |
| **Three.js (React)** | `react-three-fiber` | `web3d-integration-patterns` | — |
| **3D authoring export** | `blender-web-pipeline` | `spline-interactive`, `rive-interactive` | — |
| **React / Next perf** | `vercel-react-best-practices` | `vercel-composition-patterns` | — |
| **Vercel deploy / cost** | `deploy-to-vercel`, `vercel-optimize` | `vercel-cli-with-tokens` | — |
| **Documents** | `docx`, `pdf`, `pptx`, `xlsx` | — | — |
| **Create skills** | Anthropic `skill-creator` | — | — |
| **MCP authoring** | `mcp-builder` | — | — |
| **E2E / UI test** | `webapp-testing` | — | — |
| **Docs prose review** | `writing-guidelines` | vibeCodingRules `writing-style.mdc` | — |

