## MCP vs Skill

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Search/install 21st components | 21st MCP (`21st` in MCP panel) |
| Browse shadcn source/demos | `shadcn-ui` MCP |
| Install shadcn into repo | `npx shadcn@latest mcp init` in that project + CLI |
| Design tokens / palettes / UX rules | `ui-ux-pro-max` skill (Python search script) |
| Animation API correctness | Official GSAP skills |

---

## Noise Reduction

Removed globally (duplicates / non-production): `template-skill`, `design-taste-frontend-v1`, `gpt-taste`, claudedesign `skill-creator`, claudedesign `gsap-scrolltrigger`, `web-artifacts-builder`, `internal-comms`, `slack-gif-creator`. Official GSAP `gsap-scrolltrigger` reinstalled from greensock/gsap-skills.

Keep advanced packs (3D, motion, Taste style variants, imagegen) for daily unique site work.

---

## Agent Behavior

1. Match task to **one primary** row in the matrix.
2. **Read** that skill's `SKILL.md` before implementing (do not answer from memory for GSAP, shadcn, or design-system generation).
3. **New / unique / out-of-the-box UI** (user did not name a library): read `ui-ux-pro-max` first; if output still feels generic, also read `design-taste-frontend`. Style hints: antique/vintage → `minimalist-ui` or `high-end-visual-design`; bold/raw → `industrial-brutalist-ui`.
4. **Name conflicts:** if user says "use Taste" → `design-taste-frontend`; "use UI UX Pro Max" → `ui-ux-pro-max`; "official GSAP" → greensock pack.
5. **Stack detection:** React + 3D → `react-three-fiber`; vanilla 3D → `threejs-webgl`; Next.js perf → Vercel skills first.
